  story:[ "<b>The street is an excavation now.</b> A torn pipe section rests beside soil samples, coating fragments, and a time-stamped pressure trace.", "Line-Walker Dumas, The Dispatcher, and The Clerk can move the inquiry from the right-of-way to the control screen and finally into the integrity schedule.", "The case keeps offering <b>Sabotage or a third-party strike</b> and <b>A freak ground shift — an act of God</b>. Both are faster than measuring the metal that remains.", "Gas service is running through a temporary bypass. In eight days, the operator intends to restore normal pressure across the district." ],
  endings:{ overclaimWhat:"attack", dismissalWhat:"freak",
    win:{ expertTitle:"The Wall-Loss Case Completed", expert:["You identify <b>Hollis Trask — pipeline operator</b>, <b>The Operator's Integrity Office</b>, and <b>Advanced corrosion with the inline inspection skipped</b>. Not sabotage or a third-party strike. Not a freak ground shift — an act of god. Pit geometry, coating failure, pressure history, and the cancelled tool run fit one integrity sequence.","Your reconstruction explains why ordinary operating pressure ruptured an extraordinary local flaw rather than a sound section of pipe."], soundTitle:"A Pressure-Tight Finding", sound:["You connect <b>Hollis Trask — pipeline operator</b>, <b>The Operator's Integrity Office</b>, and <b>Advanced corrosion with the inline inspection skipped</b>. The corrosion argument is persuasive, though growth rate and fracture margin are lightly treated.","The pipeline board accepts the conclusion because field metal measurements and integrity scheduling records independently support it."], namedTitle:"The Integrity Failure Named", named:["You choose <b>Hollis Trask — pipeline operator</b>, <b>The Operator's Integrity Office</b>, and <b>Advanced corrosion with the inline inspection skipped</b>, but provide little detail on how the flaw reached critical size.","The accusation stands; pressure restoration still requires a fuller fitness-for-service assessment along the affected segment."] },
    overclaim:{ title:"A Strike Story Misses the Metal", body:["You select <b>Sabotage or a third-party strike</b>, although the fracture surface, corrosion products, and absent tool inspection do not resemble fresh external damage.","The sabotage claim distracts from <b>Advanced corrosion with the inline inspection skipped</b>, the integrity finding that can be measured directly on the recovered pipe."] },
    dismissal:{ title:"Ground Movement Becomes a Shortcut", body:["You accept <b>A freak ground shift — an act of God</b>, letting a general geologic possibility substitute for the specific wall loss present at rupture.","That answer allows continued pressure service without correcting the inspection gap that left the defect unknown."] },
    wrongNames:{ title:"Correct Corrosion, Wrong Integrity Trail", body:["You establish <b>Advanced corrosion with the inline inspection skipped</b> but assign the controlling decision or records incorrectly. The line history ultimately reaches"] } },
